{{Information
|description={{et|1=Vesilest (''Hydrachnidia'') külgvaates pildistatud mikroskoobi all kasutades 8x objektiivi. Isend on kogutud 2023. aasta mais. Vesilestade näol on tegu ühe kõige mitmekesisema ja arvukama veeselgrootute rühma esindajaga. Külgvaade toob eriti hästi esile vesilestadele iseloomuliku kerakujulise keha, mille läbikumav pind omab kaunist sinakat-rohelist helki. Selgelt eristuvad ka jäsemed oma iseloomulike ogajate harjastega.
Pilt on tehtud musta tausta peal, mis toob esile looma poolläbipaistva kehapinna tekstuuri ja jäsemete peened detailid. Valgustamisel on kasutatud peegelduvat valgust fotograafia välklambilt (''speedlight''), mis rõhutab eriti hästi isendi välispinna struktuure ja metalselt helkivat kesta. Pilt on tehtud kasutades fookuse virnastamise tehnikat (''focus stacking''), mis tagab suure teravussügavuse.}}
{{en|1=A water mite (Hydrachnidia) photographed in lateral view under a microscope using an 8x objective. The specimen was collected in May 2023. Water mites represent one of the most diverse and abundant groups of aquatic invertebrates. The lateral view particularly emphasizes the characteristic spherical body of water mites, with its translucent surface displaying a beautiful bluish-green iridescence. The limbs with their distinctive spiny bristles are also clearly visible.
The specimen was photographed against a black background, which excellently highlights the texture of the semi-transparent body surface and the fine details of the appendages. The lighting technique used was reflected light from a photographic speedlight flash, which particularly emphasizes the surface structures and metallic sheen of the carapace. The image was created using focus stacking technique, which ensures great depth of field throughout the subject.}}
